  checkpoint {
    user_intent: "Portfolio Architect Prompt Creation\nThe user\'s goal is to create a comprehensive prompt for AI Studio that synthesizes various resume versions into a cohesive professional portfolio. This involves defining the AI\'s role, the task of designing a portfolio structure and content, blending brand identities, specifying portfolio sections (Hero, About Me, Skills, Projects, Experience, Footer), and outlining the desired output format (color palette, typography, copy, and React/Tailwind CSS code). The user also wants to ensure the prompt effectively highlights their unique skills and is ready for coding."
    intent_only: true
    included_step_index_end: 10
    conversation_log_uris: "file:///.gemini/antigravity/brain/2e1eeb76-7069-4f9f-8457-10d46db506f8/.system_generated/logs/overview.txt"
    user_requests: "Here is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^1.29.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.1.14\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^5.0.4\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.0\nreact-dom: ^19.0.0\nvite: ^6.2.0\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\ntailwindcss: ^4.1.14\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ~5.8.2\nvite: ^6.2.0\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": []\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {StrictMode} from \'react\';\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(\n  <StrictMode>\n    <App />\n  </StrictMode>,\n);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig, loadEnv} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(({mode}) => {\n  const env = loadEnv(mode, \'.\', \'\');\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    define: {\n      \'process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY\': JSON.stringify(env.GEMINI_API_KEY),\n    },\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\303\242\302\200\302\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
    user_requests: "To create a high-quality portfolio in AI Studio, you need a prompt that tells the AI exactly how to synthesize your various resume versions\342\200\224which range from **Prompt Engineering** to **Full-Stack AI**\342\200\224into a cohesive professional brand.\n\nHere is a comprehensive prompt you can use. Copy and paste the entire block below into AI Studio.\n\n---\n\n### **The Portfolio Architect Prompt**\n\n**Role:** You are an expert Full-Stack Developer and Portfolio Designer. \n**Task:** Using the provided resume data for Vivek Dalvi, design a high-end, professional personal portfolio website structure and content.\n\n**Brand Identity to Blend:**\n1.  [cite_start]**The AI Specialist:** Focus on Agentic AI, RAG pipelines, and LLM integration (LangChain, Gemini API)[cite: 7, 26, 45, 47].\n2.  [cite_start]**The Engineer:** Highlight the production-grade internship at DSW, focusing on PII detection and encryption[cite: 16, 18, 81, 83].\n3.  [cite_start]**The Creative Technologist:** Showcase the ability to bridge natural language and media (EduDiff math animations)[cite: 50, 52, 107].\n\n**Portfolio Structure Required:**\n* [cite_start]**Hero Section:** A punchy tagline that combines \"Computer Science (AI & ML) Student\" with \"Agentic AI & Full-Stack Developer\"[cite: 6, 76].\n* [cite_start]**About Me:** Synthesize his 8.4 CGPA at A.P. Shah Institute, his Honors in Cyber Security, and his passion for solving real-world problems with automation[cite: 12, 73, 139].\n* **Technical Bento Box (Skills):** Categorize skills into: \n    * [cite_start]**Languages:** Python, Java, C++, JavaScript[cite: 148].\n    * [cite_start]**AI/LLM Stack:** LangChain, RAG, Agentic AI, Gemini API, OpenAI/Llama 3[cite: 26, 46, 179].\n    * [cite_start]**Dev Tools:** Docker, K8s, FastAPI, React.js, and ClickHouse[cite: 31, 33, 49, 94].\n* **Selected Works (Deep Dive):**\n    1.  [cite_start]**CampusPal:** Emphasize the 5-layer hallucination control system and RAG-web search routing[cite: 48, 104].\n    2.  [cite_start]**EduDiff:** Highlight the prompt-to-code workflow using Gemini 2.5 Flash and Manim[cite: 52, 109].\n    3.  [cite_start]**TransactAI:** Focus on the \"Production Build\" aspect using DistilBERT[cite: 55, 57, 113].\n* [cite_start]**Experience Timeline:** Detail the DSW internship, specifically the implementation of Microsoft Presidio for data privacy[cite: 18, 135].\n* [cite_start]**Footer:** Include links to GitHub (Vivek5143) and LinkedIn (vivek-dalvi5143)[cite: 5, 126, 127].\n\n**Output Format:**\n1.  Provide a suggested **color palette** and **typography** (e.g., Dark Mode, Cyber-minimalism).\n2.  Write the **full copy** for each section in a professional yet innovative tone.\n3.  Provide the **React/Tailwind CSS code** for a responsive one-page layout that implements this design.\n\n---\n\n### **Why this works for you:**\n* [cite_start]**It captures your specific edge:** Instead of just saying \"I code,\" it highlights high-level concepts like **hallucination defense systems** and **PII encryption**[cite: 48, 83].\n* [cite_start]**It utilizes all resumes:** It pulls your Java skills from one resume [cite: 148] [cite_start]and your specific Gemini 2.5 Flash experience from another[cite: 109].\n* **It\342\200\231s Ready-to-Code:** By asking for React and Tailwind code, you can immediately deploy this to Vercel or GitHub Pages.\n\n**Would you like me to help you refine the \"Hero Statement\" or write a specific \"About Me\" bio based on these details first?**\n"
    user_requests: "To create a high-quality portfolio in AI Studio, you need a prompt that tells the AI exactly how to synthesize your various resume versions\342\200\224which range from **Prompt Engineering** to **Full-Stack AI**\342\200\224into a cohesive professional brand.\n\nHere is a comprehensive prompt you can use. Copy and paste the entire block below into AI Studio.\n\n---\n\n### **The Portfolio Architect Prompt**\n\n**Role:** You are an expert Full-Stack Developer and Portfolio Designer. \n**Task:** Using the provided resume data for Vivek Dalvi, design a high-end, professional personal portfolio website structure and content.\n\n**Brand Identity to Blend:**\n1.  [cite_start]**The AI Specialist:** Focus on Agentic AI, RAG pipelines, and LLM integration (LangChain, Gemini API)[cite: 7, 26, 45, 47].\n2.  [cite_start]**The Engineer:** Highlight the production-grade internship at DSW, focusing on PII detection and encryption[cite: 16, 18, 81, 83].\n3.  [cite_start]**The Creative Technologist:** Showcase the ability to bridge natural language and media (EduDiff math animations)[cite: 50, 52, 107].\n\n**Portfolio Structure Required:**\n* [cite_start]**Hero Section:** A punchy tagline that combines \"Computer Science (AI & ML) Student\" with \"Agentic AI & Full-Stack Developer\"[cite: 6, 76].\n* [cite_start]**About Me:** Synthesize his 8.4 CGPA at A.P. Shah Institute, his Honors in Cyber Security, and his passion for solving real-world problems with automation[cite: 12, 73, 139].\n* **Technical Bento Box (Skills):** Categorize skills into: \n    * [cite_start]**Languages:** Python, Java, C++, JavaScript[cite: 148].\n    * [cite_start]**AI/LLM Stack:** LangChain, RAG, Agentic AI, Gemini API, OpenAI/Llama 3[cite: 26, 46, 179].\n    * [cite_start]**Dev Tools:** Docker, K8s, FastAPI, React.js, and ClickHouse[cite: 31, 33, 49, 94].\n* **Selected Works (Deep Dive):**\n    1.  [cite_start]**CampusPal:** Emphasize the 5-layer hallucination control system and RAG-web search routing[cite: 48, 104].\n    2.  [cite_start]**EduDiff:** Highlight the prompt-to-code workflow using Gemini 2.5 Flash and Manim[cite: 52, 109].\n    3.  [cite_start]**TransactAI:** Focus on the \"Production Build\" aspect using DistilBERT[cite: 55, 57, 113].\n* [cite_start]**Experience Timeline:** Detail the DSW internship, specifically the implementation of Microsoft Presidio for data privacy[cite: 18, 135].\n* [cite_start]**Footer:** Include links to GitHub (Vivek5143) and LinkedIn (vivek-dalvi5143)[cite: 5, 126, 127].\n\n**Output Format:**\n1.  Provide a suggested **color palette** and **typography** (e.g., Dark Mode, Cyber-minimalism).\n2.  Write the **full copy** for each section in a professional yet innovative tone.\n3.  Provide the **React/Tailwind CSS code** for a responsive one-page layout that implements this design.\n\n---\n\n### **Why this works for you:**\n* [cite_start]**It captures your specific edge:** Instead of just saying \"I code,\" it highlights high-level concepts like **hallucination defense systems** and **PII encryption**[cite: 48, 83].\n* [cite_start]**It utilizes all resumes:** It pulls your Java skills from one resume [cite: 148] [cite_start]and your specific Gemini 2.5 Flash experience from another[cite: 109].\n* **It\342\200\231s Ready-to-Code:** By asking for React and Tailwind code, you can immediately deploy this to Vercel or GitHub Pages.\n\n**Would you like me to help you refine the \"Hero Statement\" or write a specific \"About Me\" bio based on these details first?**\n"
  }
}
