  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Revising Project Integration**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating the projects into an ultra-premium, interactive bento dashboard, keeping full support for Apple/Linear design. I\'m also reviewing the user\'s initial request for a rewrite, as I\'ve confirmed perfect project summaries are already available in `constants.ts`.\n\n\n**Designing Portfolio Concept**\n\nI\'m now generating initial design concepts for a world-class, Apple-inspired personal portfolio. It\'s becoming clearer: a dark, premium theme with purple, blue, and emerald accents is the foundation. I\'m focusing on glassmorphism cards with rounded corners, animated gradient blobs, and smooth transitions. The split-screen hero will have an AI-driven diagram on the right, and bio milestones on the \"About Me\" section. The tech stack will be an interactive bento grid.\n\n\n**Exploring Interactive Visuals**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into interactive project presentations. Instead of static cards, I\'m envisioning micro-apps and widgets. CampusPal gets a real-time RAG response simulator; EduDiff, a prompt-to-video visualization with animated math; TransactAI, a dynamic spending chart mockup; and InstaClaim, an OCR invoice scanner interface.\n\n\n**Envisioning Interactive Mockups**\n\nI\'m now sketching out interactive portfolio mockups with animated CrewAI flows as log consoles. My focus is a CrewAI animation: Planner, Researcher, Code Reviewer discussing a visual design, and real-time outputs. Daily Work Logger features a \"Parse Log\" button that turns unstructured text into a JSON log synced with a Google Sheet UI. The Interview Assistant gets a simulated voice assistant with answer selection and real-time AI feedback. I\'m excited; this feels like a living software lab! I\'ll be doing research on Tailwind imports next.\n\n\n**Defining Visual Foundations**\n\nI\'m now fully defining the visual foundations. I\'ve successfully imported the \"Sora\" font and configured the CSS to use it for headings alongside \"Inter\" and \"JetBrains Mono\" for code. I\'m now sketching out interactive widget concepts, with detailed RAG chat simulations for CampusPal and animated math renderers for EduDiff.\n\n\n**Developing Interactive Interface Concepts**\n\nI\'m now iterating on interactive concepts. I\'m focusing on dynamic visualizations: a math-rendering triangle with a formula overlay for EduDiff. TransactAI is evolving into a dynamic spending dashboard with SMS alerts and chart simulations. InstaClaim features an offline RAG scanner with black and gold UI. Multi-Agent Platform now features an interactive node chart, displaying a node chart with logs for Agent workflows. The Daily Work Logger parses unstructured text into categorized cards that sync to a Google Sheet.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 10
      nanos: 555594699
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
