  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Envisioning the Rewrite**\n\nI\'ve got a complete understanding of `src/App.tsx` now. My focus is on a complete rewrite. The goal is a truly unique layout. The plan includes a mouse position halo (or smooth, animated nodes) for the background, a top bar with a progress indicator, and fully custom, interactive widgets. I\'m excited by the possibilities.\n\n\n**Defining Project Previews**\n\nI\'m now detailing interactive project previews to simulate app interactions beautifully. I envision polished elements, cards, and state changes. I\'m focusing on an elegant Bento Grid for skills, a \"GitHub Stats Simulator,\" and an animated experience timeline. I\'m excited to refine the education and contact sections. I\'ll make a custom section for each project to render these previews!\n\n\n**Designing Interactive Simulations**\n\nI\'m deep in designing simulations for each project. For CampusPal, I\'m visualizing a mini-chat window with a dot-matrix typing effect simulating RAG processing. EduDiff will feature a dynamic canvas rendering SVG transformations of equations, while TransactAI will showcase a sleek financial chart and interactive SMS alerts. I\'m focusing on user immersion and intuitive interactions.\n\n\n**Crafting Detailed Simulations**\n\nI\'m now building out detailed simulations for those projects. For the HDFC Bank example, I\'m simulating a transaction, complete with alert fly-ins, category assignments, and a dynamic spending chart. InstaClaim is getting a luxury dashboard showcasing offline LLM parsing, with an OCR mock process and structured table generation. I\'m focusing on user interaction with these simulations. I\'m also planning the multi-agent platform simulation - a CrewAI workflow diagram with pulsing tokens.\n\n\n**Developing Interactive Components**\n\nI\'m now detailing an \"editor window\" component. It will feature a raw text input for logging work, with a \"Parse to Google Sheets\" button. The parser, upon click, extracts key metrics into an interactive spreadsheet table row. Then I\'m thinking about a \"Voice-Based Interview Simulator\", in a dark cockpit style. I envision responsive voice bars with an AI interviewer. The recruiter selects response options, dynamically adjusting real-time AI critique dials.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
