  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Hover Visuals**\n\nOkay, so I\'ve pinned down the data schema, that\'s done. Now I\'m shifting gears, digging into those Antigravity hover effects. The aim is to understand what gives them that signature feel, and I\'ve started breaking down the key elements: dynamic card borders that react to mouse position, and that subtle 3D tilt.\n\n\n**Designing Spotlight Card**\n\nI\'m focused on designing the `SpotlightCard` component using React hooks, `useRef`, and Framer Motion. I\'m thinking about how the Antigravity spotlight card works specifically. I\'m planning to track mouse coordinates within the card using `onMouseMove`, utilizing `useMotionValue` for better performance. I need to understand how `motion/react` with `useMotionValue` and `useMotionTemplate` works, so I can start by creating the wrapper component at `/src/components/SpotlightCard.tsx` using `create_file`.\n\n\n**Implementing Mouse Tracking**\n\nI\'ve got the mouse tracking dialed in now using `useMotionValue`. The `onMouseMove` handler is calculating mouse position relative to the card, updating `mouseX` and `mouseY` within the React component. I\'m exploring a radial gradient with a dynamic center based on those motion values for an animated spotlight. Also, I\'m thinking of overlaying a simulated 3D tilt, leveraging `useTransform` to translate mouse coordinates into rotation values for that parallax effect.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 11
      nanos: 676729564
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
